  "origin": "A collection (version 0.1.3) of openly-licensed instruction-tuning datasets for Danish (and English, French, German, Italian), built using the Dynaword approach. 4.40M samples, 2.85B Llama-3 tokens across 8 task types: general, translation, reasoning, refusal, code, tool_use, instruction_following, qa. Sub-sources include apertus-sft-mixture (ODC-By, 2.30B), wiki-instruct-da (Unknown license, 190M), wildchat-qwen (CC-BY 4.0, 172M), translation-100k (CC-BY-SA 4.0, 101M), agentic-code-sft-mix-v1 (CC-BY 4.0, 59M), danish-verifiable-reasoning (CC-BY 4.0, 16M), mt-da-deepseek (CC-BY 4.0, 9M), when2call (CC-BY 4.0), ifbench-train (Unknown), and da-refusals (CC-BY 4.0). Because sub-sources carry different licenses, the overall license is stated as the dominant ODC-By; downstream consumers must consult per-sub-source datasheets. Form: reformatted. Contributed 3.54B sampled tokens per epoch to the DFM Mimir v1 corpus (5.03%). Post-training complement to Danish Dynaword, part of the Danish Foundation Models initiative (foundationmodels.dk).",
